From b78236f4498153135487346cc6566f1b8b0c4039 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 18:05:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04519/11362] [outer-loop] Build GAP-4890 single-positive
 goal-energy operator: clears the win-exemplar floor; surfaces the deeper
 goal-REPRESENTATION ceiling (GAP-4891)

Operator "build it next" -> the GAP-4890 unblock for within-game L2->L3 deepening.

NEW OPERATOR: induce_goal_energy_single_positive(win_grid, non_win_grids) in
arc_agi3_goal_induction.py. The >=2-win floor in induce_goal_energy was conservatism, not
necessity (H1/H3/H4 only use the win value + the non-win distribution). The new operator
fires from ONE win iff it is STRICTLY separated from every negative on a feature (the
anti-mis-induction guard, just with 1 positive), else returns None. Same energy(grid)->float
contract, drops into the graph_explore_solve_v2 goal_energy hook. 4 unit tests
(test_arc_single_positive_goal_energy.py): fires-where-2win-floor-blocks, none-when-no-
separation, colour-reduction, empty-inputs. All pass; adversarial_verify clean.

REAL-DATA RESULT (the layered finding): the operator CLEARS the win-exemplar floor (it now
attempts induction from the lone L_k-completion exemplar), but on ALL 4 grid-based stalled
games (cd82, sk48, sp80, cn04) it returns None -- NO object/colour-COUNT feature separates
the win from non-wins. These games' goals are SPATIAL/VALUE/ORDER (region-fill, color-reorder,
placement, alignment), not count. So the binding ceiling on multi-level deepening is NOT the
win-exemplar floor (now addressed) but the goal-induction REPRESENTATION -> logged as GAP-4891
(high): a richer goal-feature family (cell-value/mask match, spatial alignment, order) is the
next unblock; the change-location prior supplies the mask, the gap is the value/spatial
predicate over it. GAP-4890 status -> building (floor addressed); evidence in
results/arc_within_game_l3_self_induction_{cd82,sk48,sp80,cn04}_stage1.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
